**Sprint Room Reporting**

Monthly Process Reference

*Team handover **&** reference document*

This document walks through the full monthly Sprint Room reporting workflow for Ford carlines (Capri, Explorer, Kuga, Puma). It is structured as six sequential phases. Each phase opens with a banner summarising the goal, then breaks down into numbered steps with screenshots and callouts where useful.

**Tip: **skim the *Process **at a glance* table on the next page before each new reporting cycle. The full detail follows after.

## Process at a glance

*Six phases from start to delivery. Phases 1 and 2 can be done in parallel; phases 3–6 are sequential.*

| **Phase** | **What you do** | **Where** | **Output** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **1** | Clean Brandwatch queries — check peaks & exclude noise | Brandwatch (Capri, Explorer, Kuga, Puma) | Cleaner queries before reporting starts |
| **2** | Set up the new month’s slide deck | PowerPoint (from Trello card) | Title slide updated, slide 2 ready for new insight |
| **3** | Clean dashboard sentiment & update charts | Brandwatch dashboard → PPT | Volume, source, sentiment charts refreshed |
| **4** | Export raw data & update semiprocess sheet | Brandwatch → Google Sheets | Pivot tables ready for both months |
| **5** | Write insights from charts & pivot tables | PPT slide + slide notes | Bulletted insight on the new month’s slide |
| **6** | Final QA & deliver | PPT, Google Sheets, Trello, email | Sent to Val (CC: Mike, Seb, Mia) |

| **BEFORE YOU BEGIN** You will need access to: **Brandwatch** (Sprint Room dashboards), **Trello** (current month card), the **semiprocess**** Google Sheets** for each carline, and the **PowerPoint deck** from the previous month. Spare **Monday AMs** and **Friday PMs** before month-end are good slots for getting ahead on Phase 1, even if the full reporting month isn’t available yet. |
| --- |

| **PHASE ****1  ·****  ****Brandwatch**** — clean the queries** *Inspect each carline’s search query for the reporting month, identify irrelevant content, and add it to the **boolean** exclusions.* |
| --- |

Run this for **all four carlines** (Capri, Explorer, Kuga, Puma) before reporting work begins.

### Step-by-step

- Open the query for the carline in Brandwatch and set the date range to the reporting month.

- Click into **each visible peak** in the Mention Volume chart and inspect the items — ideally check every date, not just peaks.

- Note any **key phrases** from titles or text snippets of irrelevant items (in the original language).

- Once you’ve been through the whole month, add those phrases to the boolean exclusions. Wait for Brandwatch to update, then repeat to catch anything missed.

*Figure 1.1 — **Brandwatch** Explorer query. The peak around 11 March is the kind of spike to click into and verify.*

| **DON’T UPDATE THE BOOLEAN PER-PEAK** Wait until you have checked **all** identified peaks (or all dates) before updating exclusions. Updating mid-pass means waiting for Brandwatch to refresh between each change — batch them. |
| --- |

| **PHASE ****2  ·****  ****Set up the new month’s deck** *Pull last month’s deck from Trello and prep slides 1–3 for the new reporting period.* |
| --- |

### Step-by-step

- Download last month’s deck from the **Trello card** (e.g. [February 2026](https://trello.com/c/BASqRuzL/88-february-sprints)).

- Edit the **title slide** to show the new reporting month and today’s date.

- Duplicate the first non-title slide — this becomes your new **slide 2**.

- On the new slide 2: update the subtitle to the new reporting period, delete the slide notes, and **mark out the old insights** (move them down a line and highlight in yellow as a reference for writing the new insight).

- On slide 3 (the former slide 2): mark this as the **previous month’s slide** — it stays in for client reference and the marking prevents confusion.

- Delete the old slide 4.

*Figure 2.1 — Slide 2 with the previous month’s insight bullets moved down and highlighted yellow, ready as reference for the new write-up.*

| **PHASE ****3  ·****  ****Clean the dashboard ****&**** update charts** *Fix sentiment tagging in the Mention List, then update the volume, source, and sentiment charts in the deck.* |
| --- |

Search **‘Ford Sprint Room’** in Brandwatch and open the relevant dashboard. Ignore Focus, Mustang Mach-E, and Puma Gen-E.

Each month is run in two passes: **Explorer + Capri** first, then **Puma + Kuga**.

### 3.1  Clean sentiment in the Mention List

*Online News is the biggest source of inaccurate sentiment data. Cleaning it up now saves you from rework at the end of the cycle.*

- Scroll to the bottom of the dashboard to find the **Mention List widget**.

*Figure 3.1 — The Mention List widget at the bottom of the dashboard.*

- Set filters: **Ford model** (the carline you’re reporting on), **Online News** as content source, and **positive + negative** sentiment.

*Figure 3.2 — Filter panel set to Ford model + Online News + positive/negative sentiment only.*

- Screen each result for relevance to the carline and accuracy of its sentiment tag. **Tip:** export the widget as Excel and work in Google Sheets so you can use **=****GOOGLETRANSLATE(****)** on foreign-language items.

- For any item that doesn’t specifically focus on the filtered carline, change it to **neutral**. This includes passing mentions, articles covering several carlines equally, and articles focused on a different carline of the same brand.

*Figure 3.3 — Re-tagging an item as neutral via the sentiment dropdown on the mention.*

- If an item is tagged positive but is clearly negative (or vice versa), correct it the same way.

- Delete blatantly irrelevant items.

*Figure 3.4 — Deleting an irrelevant item from the Mention List.*

| **ALL PASSING MENTIONS = NEUTRAL** Val is hawkish on this. Any sentiment changes you make here **must** be reflected both in your charts *and* in Brandwatch (use the item filter widget at the bottom of each dashboard). Pre-empt this and you save yourself a round trip. |
| --- |

### 3.2  Update each chart in Brandwatch

Once the data is clean, set the date scope on each chart and save the dashboard before exporting.

- **Volume over time chart: **reporting month + previous 3 months.

- **Source of mentions chart: **reporting month only.

- **Sentiment of mentions chart: **reporting month only.

| **SAVE THE DASHBOARD** **Once chart scopes are set, save the dashboard before you start exporting. Easy to miss — painful to redo.** |
| --- |

Now export each chart as Excel and update the corresponding charts in your reporting-month slide. The detail per chart is below.

### 3.3  Volume over time chart

- Open the chart’s linked data in PowerPoint.

- Copy the existing charted data into the reference table on the right.

- Move the newer three months’ data to the left, leaving space on the right for the new month.

| **DON’T OVERWRITE THE AVERAGE ROW** The Average row contains formulae. Leave it alone when shifting data left. |
| --- |

*Figure 3.5 — Volume over time chart data table in PPT, with the reference table on the right.*

### 3.4  Source of mentions pie charts

These can be copied straight from Brandwatch — you don’t even need to export. Hover over each segment to read the raw figure, or use the ‘Breakdown by’ dropdown to switch chart type.

*Figure 3.6 — The ‘Breakdown by’ dropdown lets you switch chart types directly in **Brandwatch**.*

### 3.5  Sentiment of mentions chart

This is the fiddliest of the three. The left-hand tables are editable; the right-hand tables are formulated — don’t touch them.

- Each block on the left needs to move down one position — *except* the bottom (third) block, which is being replaced.

- Copy & paste-as-values: red section → bottom table; green section → red section.

- Export the Brandwatch sentiment chart for the reporting period and paste into the now-empty top block.

- Update the month label in the top-left of the new table.

*Figure 3.7 — Sentiment chart data tables. Red → bottom, green → red, then paste fresh export into the top.*

| **CHECK MODEL ORDER BEFORE YOU PASTE** Brandwatch exports do **not** always list models in the same order as the chart’s table. Verify each row matches its model label before pasting values. |
| --- |

| **PHASE ****4  ·****  ****Export raw data ****&**** update the ****semiprocess**** sheet** *Pull each competitor’s data download from **Brandwatch** into the Google Sheets **semiprocess** document and refresh the pivot tables.* |
| --- |

### 4.1  Export from Brandwatch

- Scroll to the top of the dashboard and find the volume-per-month line chart.

- Click each competitor’s datapoint for the reporting month (**including Ford**).

- In the pop-up: **Export** → **Data Download** → **Next Step** → **Start Download**. No settings need changing.

- Repeat for every competitor.

- A green bar appears at the top — click **Excel** (***not*** CSV) for each download until the bar disappears.

*Figure 4.1 — Clicking a competitor datapoint (e.g. **Enyaq** Coupe) opens the export pop-up. Use Data Download → Excel.*

### 4.2  Paste into the semiprocess

- Open the relevant carline’s **semiprocess**** Google Sheet** and go to the **Raw Data – Updated** tab.

- Paste each export into the bottom-most free space of the **Query Id** column (column D).

- Sheets can be slow — hold **Ctrl+V** for ~10 seconds to avoid clipboard misreads.

### 4.3  Extend the helper formulas

Columns A and B are formulated for use in the pivot tables:

- Column A: =MONTH(F[row])

- Column B: =GOOGLETRANSLATE(G[row])

- Scroll to the bottom of your new data.

- Select all the empty red cells in columns A and B, going up to **include the two filled cells** from the previous month’s last row.

- Press **Ctrl+D** to fill the formulas down. Sheets may lag for a few minutes.

*Figure 4.2 — Selecting from the bottom of new data up through the last filled formula cell, ready for **Ctrl+D**.*

### 4.4  Archive the oldest month

The semiprocess holds two months at a time. After adding the new one, push the oldest to archive.

- Filter the data to show only the oldest input month (e.g. for the March 2026 Puma file, that’s month = 1, January).

- Select all of the oldest month’s data and copy.

- Open **Raw Data – Archive** from the All Sheets menu (bottom-left), scroll to the bottom, and paste.

- Return to **Raw Data – Updated** and **delete the rows** for the archived month — don’t just clear contents, delete the rows themselves so no blanks are left.

| **DELETE ROWS, DON’T CLEAR THEM** Blank rows get caught by the data filter and break the pivots. Always use **Delete row**, never *Delete* on cell contents. |
| --- |

### 4.5  Update the pivot tables

- Go into each **process file** tab.

- Update each of the 5 pivot tables per tab so their range covers **both** months.

- You may need to insert extra rows so the pivots have room to display the new data.

| **PHASE ****5  ·****  ****Write the insights** *Use the charts and pivot tables to write the new month’s narrative — in-slide bullets plus slide notes for overflow.* |
| --- |

Insights are split between the **in-slide text box** and the **slide notes**. Use the notes for overflow: extra mentions drivers, country breakdowns, etc.

| **COUNTRY BREAKDOWNS IN THE NOTES** Val is especially interested in country breakdowns of platform mentions. These are usually too bulky for the main slide, so keep them in the notes. **Heuristic:** break a story down by country if it has more than ~30 mentions in any single country. |
| --- |

### Bullet structure

- **Bullet 1: **Overall volume trend for each competitor — quantify mentions, starting with Ford. Use brand + model name in the first bullet, then just the model name thereafter.

- **Bullet 2: **Key mentions drivers for Ford — give the top driver by platform (often news or forums). Then add the same for the competitor with the largest volume growth. See the relevant Process File tab.

- **Bullet 3: **Ford carline sentiment — only if there’s anything specific to mention, including ‘clusters’ (drivers with volume <30).

| **WHEN THERE ARE NO CLUSTERS** If volume for any given driver is too small (<30), use Val’s exact phrasing: ***“no clusters of issues were identified as drivers”***. |
| --- |

### Competitor changes

Also write insights for any **competitor lines with major changes** (positive or negative) since the previous month — but **only** the major ones. If there isn’t room in the main slide, put them in the notes.

### A note on sentiment

All passing mentions **must** be neutral. If you change a sentiment tag, that change must show up in **both** the chart *and* Brandwatch (item filter widget at the bottom of each dashboard). Val will catch this if you don’t.

| **PHASE ****6  ·****  ****Finalise ****&**** deliver** *QA the deck against **Brandwatch** and the **semiprocess**, tidy the sheet, then upload and email.* |
| --- |

### QA checklist

- Data is consistent across charts, Brandwatch, and the semiprocess (Val will check this).

- New insight slide subtitle shows the correct month.

- PPT title slide shows the correct month and **current reporting date**.

### Tidy the semiprocess

- Refilter the current data tab to show **both months**.

- Deselect any filters on carline, content source, sentiment, etc.

- Delete any extra columns made during analysis (e.g. theme notes).

- Re-hide column C (translated full text) for neatness.

- Click **Share** → set to **anyone with the link can edit**.

### Deliver

- Save the PPT and upload it to the new **Trello card**.

- Copy the semiprocess URL into the Trello card details.

- Email to **Val**, CC **Mike, Seb, and Mia**.

*Figure 6.1 — Trello card / share view: confirm the deck is uploaded and the **semiprocess** link is in the card details.*

# Glossary & key terms

*Internal jargon used throughout this document.*

| **Sprint Room** | The Brandwatch dashboard set used for Ford monthly reporting. Search ‘Ford Sprint Room’ to find the relevant dashboards. |
| --- | --- |

| **Carline** | A specific Ford model line. The four in scope are Capri, Explorer, Kuga, and Puma. (Focus, Mustang Mach-E, and Puma Gen-E are out of scope.) |
| --- | --- |

| **Boolean exclusions** | Phrase-level exclusions added to a Brandwatch query to filter out irrelevant content surfaced in peak-checking. |
| --- | --- |

| **Mention List widget** | The widget at the bottom of each Brandwatch dashboard listing individual mentions. Used for sentiment cleanup. |
| --- | --- |

| **Semiprocess** | The per-carline Google Sheets workbook that holds raw data, helper formulas, and pivot tables. Two tabs of note: Raw Data – Updated and Raw Data – Archive. |
| --- | --- |

| **Process File tab** | A tab inside the semiprocess containing the 5 pivot tables that summarise mentions drivers by platform and carline. |
| --- | --- |

| **Cluster** | A mentions driver with a volume below ~30. Reported with the standard phrase “no clusters of issues were identified as drivers” when none qualify. |
| --- | --- |

| **Passing mention** | A mention where the carline is referenced but isn’t the focus of the article (e.g. mentioned alongside several other models). All passing mentions must be tagged neutral. |
| --- | --- |